 ### Self-Occlusion Avoidance via Offset
-Prevents a surface from sampling its own voxel contribution by offsetting the ray origin. If the offset is too large, close-by surfaces lose GI contribution; if too small, self-intersection occurs. Anisotropic voxels can solve the disconnect but require more memory [S35, unofficial].
